	•	Section 4 Comments/Quotes: Missing continuous data were imputed with the median and categorical data with the mode. Class imbalance was addressed using “over-sampling (SVM Smote) and under-sampling (Repeated Edited Nearest Neighbors).” Preprocessing was clearly described, including exclusion of non-preoperative variables, clinician review, grouping sparse categories, one-hot encoding, and standardization of continuous variables. The paper states models were trained in Python using Keras/Tensorflow but does not provide code release, so code availability is No. Table 1 gives training n=26,926 and validation n=6,731.  ￼  ￼

